<title>USA: U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,537,000 bushels.</title>
<headline>U.S. weekly soybean crush 30,537,000 bushels.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 02/05/97    01/29/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 30,537,000  30,335,000    25,785,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	 163,663     181,490	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,324,000  34,948,000    33,981,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,516,775  35,140,728	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   02/05/97    01/29/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   5,434,000   5,460,000     4,586,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    5,286,000   5,089,000     4,266,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  5,015,000   5,054,000     4,592,000</p>
<p> South Central    3,105,000   3,216,000     2,227,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  4,268,000   4,194,000     3,497,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 5,456,000   5,315,000     4,790,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,973,000   2,007,000     1,827,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	30,537,000  30,335,000    25,785,000</p>
